        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): warn when JSON5 comments are lost on config write",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw uses JSON5 to parse user configurations (supporting comments and trailing commas), but writes them back with standard JSON.stringify which silently strips all user-authored comments on every automatic config write.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nJSON5.parse discards comments during parsing - they cannot be preserved through a parse-modify-stringify roundtrip without an AST-aware library. The fix adds a warning when the original config file contains JSON5 comment markers, so users know their comments will be stripped.\n\nThe output format remains JSON.stringify (unchanged) for backward compatibility.\n\n## What Was Fixed (Review Feedback)\n\nThe initial regex `/\\/[\\/*]|^\\s*\\/\\//m` had a false positive: it matched `://` in URLs like `http://example.com` inside string values. The updated regex `/^\\s*\\/\\/|^\\s*\\/\\*/m` only matches `//` or `/*` at the start of a line, which is where JSON5 comments appear.\n\n| Input | Old regex | New regex |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|\n| `// comment` | ✅ match | ✅ match |\n| `/* block */` | ✅ match | ✅ match |\n| `\"http://url\"` | ❌ false positive | ✅ no match |\n| `{\"a\":1}` | ✅ no match | ✅ no match |\n\n## Evidence\n\n### A. Regex Validation (7/7 cases)\n\n```\n✅ \"// comment\"    -> true  (JSON5 single-line comment)\n✅ \"  // comment\"  -> true  (indented comment)\n✅ \"/* block */\"   -> true  (JSON5 block comment)\n✅ \"  /* block */\" -> true  (indented block comment)\n✅ \"\\\"http://url\\\"\" -> false (URL inside string - no false positive)\n✅ \"plain json\"    -> false (plain JSON)\n✅ \"{a:1}\"         -> false (JSON5 without comments)\n```\n\nThe regex `/^\\s*\\/\\/|^\\s*\\/\\*/m` correctly detects JSON5 comment styles without false positives on URLs or plain JSON.\n\n### B. Unit Tests (59 passed)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  59 passed (59)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/io.owner-display-secret.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n```\n\n### C. Lint + Format\n\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json src/config/io.ts -> No errors\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/config/io.ts -> All matched files use the correct format\n```\n\n### D. Code Diff\n\n```diff\n+    // Warn when the original config has JSON5 comments that will be lost\n+    if (\n+      typeof snapshot.raw === \"string\" &&\n+      !options.skipOutputLogs &&\n+      /^\\s*\\/\\/|^\\s*\\/\\*/m.test(snapshot.raw)\n+    ) {\n+      deps.logger?.warn?.(`Config write will strip JSON5 comments from ${configPath}.`);\n+    }\n```\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Does NOT preserve JSON5 comments (requires AST-aware library)\n- Only matches line-start `//` and `/*` comments; inline `/* comment */` mid-line is not detected\n- Warning fires once per config path, not on every write\n\n## Future Work\n\nFor full comment preservation, consider adding a JSON5 AST manipulation library (e.g., comment-json) or writing dynamic modifications to a separate overlay file.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- src/config/io.ts: 1 line (regex fix from `/\\/[\\/*]|^\\s*\\/\\//` to `/^\\s*\\/\\/|^\\s*\\/\\*/`)\n\nFixes #105683",
        "branch": "fix/json5-config-comment-preserve-105683",
